message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying data sources (see data_manifest.json)."
title: "CFTR Variant Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A provenance-honest, teaching-oriented walkthrough of the computational tools
  used to interpret CFTR variants: missense pathogenicity predictors, splice
  predictors, population-frequency references, and clinical/functional truth sets.
type: software
